## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical ability to diagnose multi-tenant feature-flag issues in production using Kubernetes, Redis, and tracing. It probes understanding of cache stampede, per-tenant routing, rollout safety, and latency requirements.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant feature flags and cache invalidation
- Canary rollouts and rollback safety
- Redis keyspace examination and TTL semantics
- Distributed tracing for tenant-aware requests
- Latency SLO verification under load

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo canary rollout flow
if (flagEnabledForTenant(tenant)) {
  routeToTenantService(tenant);
} else {
  routeToFallback(tenant);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for 10k tenants with dynamic flag sets?
- What rollback criteria would you codify (latency, error rate, traffic shift)?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical rate-limiting basics, a common reliability concern in public APIs. It tests per-key quotas, in-memory state, and how small designs behave under restart and burst scenarios.

## Key Concepts

- Sliding window algorithm
- Map-based per-key state
- Time-based pruning
- Testing strategy and limitations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Core limiter (simplified)
const limiter = new Map();

function allowRequest(key, now = Date.now()) {
  const windowMs = 60000;
  const limit = 60;
  const timestamps = limiter.get(key) || [];
  while (timestamps.length && timestamps[0] <= now - windowMs) timestamps.shift();
  if (timestamps.length < limit) {
    timestamps.push(now);
    limiter.set(key, timestamps);
    return true;
  }
  return false;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt for multiple instances?
- How would you test time-dependent behavior without slow sleeps?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests diagnosing certificate rotation within a service mesh, focusing on end-to-end TLS verification, per-tenant isolation, and zero-downtime deployment strategies.

## Key Concepts

- TLS certificate rotation propagation across Kubernetes secrets and Envoy proxies
- mTLS handshake troubleshooting in Istio service mesh
- Canary rollouts with automated rollback capabilities
- Per-tenant routing and isolation in multi-tenant mesh environments

## Code Example

```javascript
// TLS handshake tester (pseudo)
async function testTLS(target) {
  try {
    const response = await fetch(target);
    return response.ok;
  } catch {
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you monitor certificate expiration dates across all pods?
- What metrics would you use to detect TLS handshake failures in real-time?
- How do you ensure tenant isolation during certificate rotation?

## Why This Is Asked

Test candidate's ability to design scalable security controls for multi-tenant K8s, covering RBAC, PodSecurity, image provenance, network isolation, and policy enforcement with Gatekeeper. Expect explanation of trade-offs (complexity vs. security) and how to validate in CI.

## Key Concepts

- Least privilege RBAC per-namespace
- Pod Security Standards
- OPA Gatekeeper constraint templates
- Image provenance and signed images
- NetworkPolicy segmentation
- Audit logging and policy testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Test helper: ensures pods use allowed registries and non-root users
function isPodCompliant(pod){
  const okNamespace = pod.metadata.namespace.startsWith('team-');
  const okImage = pod.spec.containers.every(c => c.image.startsWith('registry.internal/'));
  const okUser = pod.spec.containers.every(c => c.securityContext?.runAsNonRoot === true);
  return okNamespace && okImage && okUser;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test Gatekeeper in CI/CD for new policies?
- How would you handle exception paths during incidents without breaking policy?
